x01-core-alignment patch 02-cosmic-time (git apply ignores this header)

E7 item: (d) Cosmic time.

SAGE26 behaviour: the Age (lookback-time) table is filled by time_to_present()
(R/src/core_init.c:62 for the leading z=1000 slot, R/src/core_init.c:66-67 per snapshot,
ZZ = 1/AA - 1). With GSL_FOUND (R0's binary links libgsl and imports gsl_integration_qag) it calls
gsl_integration_qag(&F, 1/(1+z), 1.0, epsabs = 1.0/Hubble, epsrel = 1.0e-9, limit 1000,
GSL_INTEG_GAUSS21, workspace of 1000) (R/src/core_init.c:159-177) on the integrand
1/sqrt(Omega/a + (1 - Omega - OmegaLambda) + OmegaLambda*a*a) (R/src/core_init.c:202-205) and returns
1.0/Hubble * result (R/src/core_init.c:195); Hubble = HUBBLE * UnitTime_in_s (R/src/core_init.c:106).

Mimic behaviour replaced: time_to_present() (src/core/init.c:202-209) integrates the same integrand
(src/core/init.c:226-235, arithmetic identical for a > 0) with the recursive adaptive Simpson rule,
absolute tolerance 1e-10 (src/util/integration.c:25-62), and returns safe_div(1.0, Hubble, 0.0) * result.
Value check (scratch program over mini-millennium.a_list, both integrators, same constants): the two
tables differ by up to 9.1e-8 relative (snapshot 0), ~1e-12 relative at later snapshots.

What the patch changes: time_to_present() calls gsl_integration_qag exactly as SAGE26 does and returns
1.0 / Hubble * result; src/core/init.c includes <gsl/gsl_integration.h>; the Makefile adds
$(shell gsl-config --cflags) to CFLAGS and $(shell gsl-config --libs) to LIBS. The integrand, the
z=1000 leading slot and the ZZ computation are unchanged (already as SAGE26).

Reading for i02: yes, it would change sage16's output (every evolution interval and time derives from
Age) and halos-only's (the core dT output is an Age difference), at the level of the table difference;
it also makes GSL a build dependency of the core.

diff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile
index fe114a22..7b1e5144 100644
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -171,6 +171,9 @@ ifdef EXTRA_LDFLAGS
     LDFLAGS += $(EXTRA_LDFLAGS)
 endif
 LIBS = -lm
+# x01 (d): SAGE26's lookback-time integrator needs GSL (gsl_integration_qag)
+CFLAGS += $(shell gsl-config --cflags)
+LIBS += $(shell gsl-config --libs)
 
 # -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 # Required Library Detection - YAML
diff --git a/src/core/init.c b/src/core/init.c
index 8de34af7..90374aef 100644
--- a/src/core/init.c
+++ b/src/core/init.c
@@ -26,6 +26,8 @@
 #include <time.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
 
+#include <gsl/gsl_integration.h>
+
 #include "config.h"
 #include "globals.h"
 #include "error.h"
@@ -200,12 +202,21 @@ void read_snap_list(void) {
  * integrated from a = 1/(1+z) to a = 1, in internal time units.
  */
 double time_to_present(double z) {
-  /* Absolute tolerance 1e-9/H gives SAGE-parity precision for lookback times
-   * of order 1/H (sage-code core_init.c used 1e-9 relative tolerance). */
-  double result = integrate_adaptive_simpson(integrand_time_to_present, NULL,
-                                             safe_div(1.0, z + 1, 1.0), 1.0, 1.0e-10, NULL);
-
-  return safe_div(1.0, MimicConfig.Hubble, 0.0) * result;
+  /* x01 (d): SAGE26's integrator (core_init.c:159-198): GSL qag, GAUSS21, workspace 1000,
+   * epsabs 1/Hubble, epsrel 1e-9, then time = 1/Hubble * result */
+  const double end_limit = 1.0;
+  const double start_limit = 1.0 / (1 + z);
+  double result, abserr;
+  gsl_function F;
+  gsl_integration_workspace *workspace = gsl_integration_workspace_alloc(1000);
+
+  F.function = &integrand_time_to_present;
+  F.params = NULL;
+  gsl_integration_qag(&F, start_limit, end_limit, 1.0 / MimicConfig.Hubble, 1.0e-9, 1000,
+                      GSL_INTEG_GAUSS21, workspace, &result, &abserr);
+  gsl_integration_workspace_free(workspace);
+
+  return 1.0 / MimicConfig.Hubble * result;
 }
 
